
             Upload Acitivities (Version 1.1) [RELEASE 2]
                 All Coding by Bobo (Mystic/X-Power)
                 -----------------------------------
                        Release date 07-31-94

Hello again, and welcome to another fine product.  This door is intended
for MULTINODE systems only and can't be used on single node systems. The
main purpouse  of this door  is to show  if a user on any other  node is
uploading something, and if so,  it tells you what's in his batch  queue
and  what  files in his  batch have  already been   finished  uploading.

Please note  that this door ONLY works  on the 32 node version of amiex!
A version  for the old /X 2.x/3.x and SExpress  will be done on request!

Notable Features:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
* WHAT is written entirely in C for fast code.
* WHAT is the fist kind of this door for amiexpress.
* WHAT have been tested and works 100% on multinode systems.
* WHAT comes in 000/020+ version to get the maximum speed on your
  system.


                              INSTALLATION
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~
WHAT requires a fully installed and running amiexpress 3.x (32 node).
It will NOT work on eairlier versions of amiexpress or S-Express.

To install WHAT, start with copying the included icon where it should be
located.

------------( Snap this lines )---------------------------
Copy RAM:Commands/BBSCmd/WHAT.info BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/
----------------------------------------------------------

Continue  with making  a directory  in doors: called 'WHAT' and copy the
main program, docs etc.

------------( Snap this lines )---------------------------
Makedir Doors:WHAT
Copy RAM:Doors/What/What.#? Doors:What/
----------------------------------------------------------

Now  copy  the executable  file 'What.<cpu>'  (depending on what CPU you
may have) to 'What.x'

(THIS IS JUST TO MAKE SURE YOU HAVE EVERYTHING INCASE YOU  LOOSE THE LHA
PACKAGE)

EG: Copy What020.x What.x
(If you have 68020+ cpu)

That's it!  Please  feel free  to contact me  if you  are having trouble
installing the tools.  My numbers  are at the  bottom of this  document.


